id: pm-todos-watcher
title: Propose stable todo source changes without applying them
description: "Watch one explicitly authorized session todo.txt file. Emit bounded revision-bound import proposals after stable writes without applying them. Acceptance: partial writes and truncation never become deletions; replacements and duplicate notifications deduplicate; shutdown preserves pending proposals. Include typed SDK and CLI, compact agent output, typed refusals with remedies, docs and public-tracker no-git validation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T16:45:21.987Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T17:21:43.483Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T16:45:37.889Z",codex-agent,"Overlap audit: installed CLI 2026.10.23 and pinned SDK 2026.10.20 provide single-invocation importer, certified complete reads, atomic writes and locks; pm-todos sessions already provide conflict-aware three-way previews. pm-observer watches transcripts and emits evidence, not todo import plans. No existing watcher item found. Reuse session reconciliation, SDK listAllComplete, acquireLock, writeFileAtomic and command output serialization. Poll only the explicit source, refuse symlinks and incomplete lines, retain omitted rows, cap input/changes/queue, persist before reporting and never apply. CI npm and Bun release checks are the full gate because host CPU is saturated."
  "2026-10-23T16:50:21.439Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses the existing session planner and public SDK complete reads, locks, atomic writes and NDJSON serialization. Default CLI performs one stable cycle and returns native TOON/JSON; follow mode streams bounded NDJSON. Queue identity includes source, session and complete tracker revisions; source and sidecar are checked again after planning. Proposals retain immutable source snapshots; queue backpressure refuses rather than discarding pending work. No source/tracker mutation or git subprocess is part of this feature."
  "2026-10-23T16:55:01.014Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public-data acceptance at public main 3008424: 94 items, 93 session-compatible and 1 unrepresentable, 195 tracker files fingerprinted. Edited source 10478 bytes, baseline sidecar 87419 bytes; 1 partial-write refusal, 1 proposed edit, 5 replacement/replay/restart duplicates suppressed, truncation retained 93 identities with zero changes, 2 pending proposals survived shutdown, zero tracker writes, unchanged source fingerprint, largest receipt 173 bytes. Run from a plain temporary directory with PATH containing no git. Initial linked test run exposed a timing-only test assumption under saturated CPU; replacing elapsed-time assertions with a deterministic monotonic test clock while retaining real file and SDK operations."
  "2026-10-23T16:56:41.495Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof passed: removing only the persisted-revision deduplication branch from TodoSourceWatcher.sample makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"watcher replacement and restart deduplicate durable revisions\" test/watcher.test.ts fail its assertion (queued instead of duplicate). Restored the function immediately. Typecheck, test-source typecheck, docstring lint (14 files, 88 declarations) and git diff --check pass. No separate ESLint configuration/script exists in this package; using its configured docstring lint and TypeScript checks."
  "2026-10-23T16:59:22.994Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted suite passed through pm test --run --progress: 18 tests passed, zero failures, skips or cancellations. Includes real installed CLI JSON/TOON output with PATH excluding git, SIGTERM shutdown retaining the durable queue, SDK concurrent-watcher deduplication, limits, conflicts and compact refusals. Public validation and behavioural revert evidence are recorded above. Full npm and Bun release checks will run in CI on the pushed head; their run URL and exact counts will be retained in the PR. Source observation is a stability heuristic; only session todo.txt is accepted and no proposal authorizes application."
  "2026-10-23T17:18:12.801Z",codex-agent,"Blocking review follow-up: JSON serialization drops undefined values from session patches, hiding field removals in saved watcher proposals. Encode removals explicitly at the watcher persistence boundary, document the representation, and add a real no-git tracker regression removing a due token. Prove the regression fails with only that encoding fix reverted, restore it, run targeted tests, typecheck and configured lint, and wait for fresh npm/Bun CI release gates. Remote feature head is unchanged and main has not advanced."
  "2026-10-23T17:21:38.662Z",codex-agent,"Blocking PR 144 finding fixed: persisted TodoProposalPatch now separates defined set values from an explicit removedFields list, so deleting due:2026-12-01 records deadline removal in proposals.json. Queue/proposal schema 2 and versioned proposal ids prevent pre-fix version 1 evidence being silently reused; legacy queues return spool_mismatch and are preserved for archival. README and SDK example document set/remove semantics and migration. Regression: watcher persists due-token removal as an explicit deadline field removal, using a real non-git SDK tracker with git absent from PATH. Isolated test passed; reverting only persistablePatches to retain undefined values and an empty removal list failed the saved deadline-removal assertion (1 failure), then the encoder was restored. Final pm test --run --progress passed both linked commands: 19 watcher tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and git diff --check passed. Fresh exact-head npm/Bun release gates will be linked with counts in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/144."
